WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.133
Agent orchestration.

2
00:00:02.433 --> 00:00:08.033
Once you have several agents, something has to decide who does what, and what happens when it fails.

3
00:00:09.233 --> 00:00:12.533
Orchestration is the control layer above your agents.

4
00:00:12.833 --> 00:00:19.467
It routes each request to the right agent, manages shared state, and handles handoffs, timeouts, and failures.

5
00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:24.533
Here is the principle that separates production systems from demos.

6
00:00:24.833 --> 00:00:26.867
Deterministic code owns the flow.

7
00:00:27.167 --> 00:00:29.467
The model owns only the judgment calls.

8
00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:32.067
Let's follow a request.

9
00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:33.533
A query arrives.

10
00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:39.867
The model's only job is to classify it, asteroid, space weather, or earth events, in one word.

11
00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:42.233
A plain dictionary looks that word up.

12
00:00:42.533 --> 00:00:46.667
And the chosen specialist runs, under a timeout that code enforces.

13
00:00:47.867 --> 00:00:49.167
Here it is in Python.

14
00:00:49.467 --> 00:00:51.467
One model call returns the route.

15
00:00:51.767 --> 00:00:54.200
A dictionary turns that route into an agent.

16
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:57.787
And the failure policy is a normal try and except.

17
00:00:57.787 --> 00:01:00.416
Never ask a model to please retry twice.

18
00:01:00.416 --> 00:01:01.533
Write a for loop.

19
00:01:02.733 --> 00:01:05.867
Here is the front door of the Orbital Research Agent.

20
00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:11.400
A FastAPI endpoint classifies each query and routes it to the right specialist.

21
00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:15.400
When the DONKI agent times out, again, the timeout is just code.

22
00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:24.167
The fallback answers from cache, and the router's unit tests still pass without a single model call, because the flow was never inside a prompt.

23
00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:26.135
Let's recap.

24
00:01:26.135 --> 00:01:30.233
Orchestration is routing, state, handoffs, and failure handling.

25
00:01:30.533 --> 00:01:33.400
Code owns the flow, and the model owns judgment.

26
00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:37.100
The model returns one word, and a dictionary dispatches.

27
00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:40.428
Retries and timeouts stay in testable code.

28
00:01:40.428 --> 00:01:43.667
Next up: supervisor and hierarchical patterns.
